From: Creeper23456 <Creeper23456@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] venus: print the runtime's error messages with
 VN_DEBUG=result

vk_errorf in the common runtime says why it failed (which feature or extension a vkCreateDevice asked for and the device does not have) only when the instance enables debug logging or a debug callback exists. A release build of the driver never printed it, so an application that gets VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT gave no hint which feature. VN_DEBUG=result already makes Venus log the results it returns; it now enables the runtime's messages too.
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_instance.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_instance.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_instance.c
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_instance.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_instance.c
@@ -283,6 +283,10 @@
       return vn_error(NULL, result);
    }
 
+   /* The common runtime explains most errors it returns (an unsupported feature or extension in
+    * vkCreateDevice, say) only when this is set or a debug callback is registered. */
+   instance->base.vk.enable_debug_logging = VN_DEBUG(RESULT);
+
    /* util_cpu_trace_init is called by vk_instance_init */
    VN_TRACE_FUNC();
 
